/*
 * Edexcel A-Level Politics (9PL0) — Multiple-Choice Question Bank
 * Keyed by component-prefixed topic id.
 * Each topic holds: { name, green: [], amber: [], red: [] }.
 * 25 questions per topic: 10 green + 10 amber + 5 red.
 * Diagnostic picks 2 green + 2 amber + 1 red = 5 MCQs at random.
 * answer: 0-based index of correct option.
 *
 * Topic ids map to the spec as follows:
 *   1.1–1.4    → Component 1 Section A, UK Politics (Political Participation)
 *   1.5–1.7    → Component 1 Section B, Core Political Ideas (all three sat)
 *   2.1–2.4    → Component 2 Section A, UK Government
 *   2.5–2.9    → Component 2 Section B, Non-core Political Ideas (ONE sat)
 *   3A.1–3A.6  → Component 3 option 3A, Comparative Politics: USA
 *   3B.1–3B.6  → Component 3 option 3B, Global Politics
 *
 * COMPONENT 3 IS A ROUTE, NOT A SET. A student sits 3A or 3B, never both, so
 * the two carry deliberately distinct ids rather than a shared 3.1–3.6. Topic
 * ids are the join key into topic_progress; if both routes used '3.1' then a
 * student who switched route would see their old USA answers resurface as
 * Global progress — RAG colours for topics they have never studied. Distinct
 * ids make a switch simply stop counting the old rows. The chosen route lives
 * in user_subjects.options ({"c3":"3A"}), added 2026-09-15.
 *
 * Either way the student sits 18 topics: 4 + 3 + 4 + 1 + 6. That is the
 * examinedTotal on the topics-config.js entry, and it does not change when a
 * student switches route.
 *
 * RED TIER. Distractors are padded to a comparable length so the correct
 * answer is not identifiable from length alone — a tell that the AQA bank's
 * red tier has throughout.
 */

